  "scope": "Existing native operation programs now carry selection_enlargement with explicit signed numeric distance and pixels/calibrated units. CurrentPlane/ActiveSelection/Planes/InPlace is closed: ranges, positions, filter options and the separate filter-calibration flag are refused. Any complete original equation is validated as immutable provenance even for disabled steps. Enabled execution applies authored choices to current stage geometry/view/X calibration; it does not replay historical geometry or navigate to captured TCZ. Metadata-only preflight advances the selection for subsequent pixel and histogram targets without sample IO, charges command working bytes/records within the existing workflow retained-byte accounting, and refuses late invalid inputs before earlier pixel reads. Detached execution publishes selection/Previous through the existing atomic transaction. Full Display dependencies are independent of paired-display publication, preserving selection-only history while refusing stale navigation. Shared Run adopts captures, offers explicit parameter fields and retains portable ordering/enable/disable/save/load and per-input batch mechanisms. Native actual input covers scalar/RGB/IEEE captured adoption, portable preparation and execution against fresh area geometry. Installed Python tests cover sequential masks, later filtering/histograms, transient history, stale state, malformed/disabled originals, resource/callback refusal and saved-session calibration per input. Existing workflow suites broaden regression coverage; no new upstream reference identities or complete-family acceptance are claimed.",
